WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.536
Have you ever had an idea and then
wondered what

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.214
you would actually do first?

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.568
Maybe you wanted to make something
useful, learn a skill,

00:00:09.568 --> 00:00:13.556
investigate a question, or improve
something around you. The challenge

00:00:13.556 --> 00:00:17.544
is finding a direction you care about
and a first

00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:19.937
step you can really learn from.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.375
In Module One, compare possible
projects. Does this matter to

00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:30.370
me? Could I realistically begin? Is the
idea focused enough

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:35.365
to make progress? Choose a direction and
explain your reasoning

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.862
in a Project Direction Brief.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.946
In Module Two, learn to plan a safe,
manageable first

00:00:42.946 --> 00:00:47.711
move. Study an example, practice
decisions, and plan an action

00:00:47.711 --> 00:00:49.618
for your own project.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.292
If you can safely attempt the action,
document what you

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:58.604
observe. If a real obstacle prevents the
attempt, describe it

00:00:58.604 --> 00:01:01.622
honestly and choose a reasonable next
step.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:06.271
You will receive feedback and make your
own decisions. Your

00:01:06.271 --> 00:01:10.562
Launch Portfolio will show your purpose,
your plan, your evidence,

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:12.278
and what you learned.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.249
You don't need special equipment, an
expensive idea, or a

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:21.918
perfect result. You need curiosity,
careful thinking, and a willingness

00:01:21.918 --> 00:01:24.253
to make your next move.

